# Rapidify AI Docker Rules

## Dockerfile Standards
- Use official base images only
- **Pin image versions** — never use `latest` tag
- Use multi-stage builds to minimize image size
- Run as non-root user in production containers
- Place frequently changing layers last (for cache efficiency)

## Docker Compose Standards
- Keep services minimal and focused
- Use `.env.example` for documenting required environment variables
- Never hardcode secrets — use environment variables or secrets management
- Pin all image versions in compose files
- Use health checks for all services

## Security
- No secrets in Dockerfiles or build args
- No sensitive data in image layers
- Scan images for vulnerabilities
- Use read-only file systems where possible

## Configuration
- Keep `.env.example` up to date with all required variables
- Document every environment variable with comments
- Use sensible defaults for non-sensitive configuration
- Separate development and production compose files when needed

## Networking
- Define explicit networks for service isolation
- Do not expose unnecessary ports
- Use internal networks for service-to-service communication

## Allowed Tooling
Docker and Docker Compose are approved by default. For new orchestration systems (Kubernetes, Nomad, etc.), explicit approval is required.
